  "id": "F1",
  "file": "scripts/review-escape-cases.ts",
  "line": 158,
  "title": "The tests must pass inside confined gates: don't canonicalize this checkout's repository from the tests",
  "detail": "Thank you: all three round-1 fixes held in review (first-parent base, acceptance-only dedupe, redacted validation fields), and the tests fail without them. The land check then blocked with 25 failures in test/review-escape-cases.test.ts, and the orchestrator reproduced them by running the file inside the real gate profile (Seatbelt, home read-denied, gate environment) from a checkout under the home: every case that calls `reviewEscapeCases` fails with `Cannot read private-strings.txt; publication blocked`. The tests' own temporary `LIMITLESS_CONFIG_DIR` is fine. The cause is `loadPrivateStrings(undefined, [resolve(import.meta.dir, \"..\")])`: `readPrivateStrings` canonicalizes the given repository root, its common directory and every linked checkout listed under `worktrees/`. Inside a gate, the other runs' checkouts are unreadable, so the call fails, and whether it fails depends on which other worktrees happen to exist (the run's own gate classified it as flaky). Make the repository roots for the private-strings check an option of `reviewEscapeCases` (default: this checkout, as today, so the CLI's behaviour is unchanged) and pass the fixture repository from the tests, so nothing outside the test's temporary directory is canonicalized. Keep everything else the tests read inside their temporary directory too (AGENTS.md, \"The home is read-denied for gates\", #500). The factory's gates run confined and will show whether this holds; don't add retries. Run only test/review-escape-cases.test.ts test/evals-cases.test.ts, `bunx biome check` on the changed files and `bunx tsc --noEmit`. Never run the full suite in a factory run (AGENTS.md)."
 }
]
